{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793571564,"nonce":"nmdE7YaWJ5BL6MsKUwBK7I2A114=","title":"cn::calendar from ashui, with events; virtual select rows; attribute-keyed CSS animations","message":"Roadmap item cn::calendar (bf7c901, P0, prereq for date_picker). Ported from ashui Calendar.hx and components.css .ui-calendar-*.\n\nCalendar\n- calendar(Signal\u003cOption\u003cCalendarDay\u003e\u003e), week_start, min_year/max_year, today, on_change. CalendarDay is month 1..=12 (ashui is 0-based; Rust convention wins). Hand-rolled civil-date math (days from epoch, Hinnant); local today via libc localtime_r / GetLocalTime / js Date. Checked for windows-msvc, wasm32, linux.\n- Parts and attributes as ashui: data-outside/today/selected/focus-visible, disabled outside years, data-step on nav; grids data-enter/data-leaving next|prev with the cn-calendar-* keyframes. Month pages are a for_each over the shown month; the old page is held by Row::on_leave until a scheduler keyframe of --duration-normal has played (scheduler clock, so headless virtual time and the window agree).\n- Keyboard after a click (GaugeFocus emulation): arrows, PageUp/Down, Home/End, Enter/Space.\n- Owner asked for metadata: CalendarEvent { day, title, kind, icon }. .events(IntoReactive\u003cVec\u003c_\u003e\u003e) marks days in place, up to 3 marks in a fixed 8px row on the cell's bottom edge (numbers must not move: owner). Dot = background, icon = color, keyed by data-kind rules. events_on() helper.\n\nSelect\n- List max 300px + scroll, opens with the chosen option centred (ScrollRef::scroll_to).\n- .virtual_rows(h): owner flagged ashui's slow-opening year dropdown, fixed there by virtualization. Rows are a for_each over a window computed from ScrollRef::watch_y (new), absolutely placed on a spacer n*h tall. Year picker uses 32px rows; 201 years build ~17 rows.\n\nEngine (blinc_layout)\n- CSS animations from rules keyed on more than one class never started (start_all_css_animations only knew #id and single-class rules), and never started when a bound attribute made a rule match. start_rule_animations at mount; eased() starts/stops when the winning animation changes. Related: 7edf49b (enter/exit keyframes).\n- ScrollRef::watch_y; dispatch_scroll_chain(_with_time) syncs the ref as a delta lands.\n- Headless harness now runs process_pending_scroll_refs at frame start, as the window does (it never ran, so ScrollRef commands were untestable headless).\n\nWorkaround\n- outline-width transitions removed from .cn-calendar-day and .cn-tree-row: an attribute-started outline transition stalls and leaves a ring behind (9d6e9c7), as the gauge already works around.\n\nOpen\n- A kind-coloured dot (.cn-calendar-event[data-kind=\"deadline\"] { background: red }) stays red on the selected day although `.cn-calendar-day[data-selected] .cn-calendar-event` is more specific. Marks are for_each rows inside the day; looks like the descendant rule is not applied to region-built rows, or loses to the later user rule. Not chased.\n- Range selection (roadmap mentions it) is not in ashui's calendar and is not done.\n- date_picker (popover + calendar) is next on the roadmap.","files":null}]}